[[WEB_SEARCHES:New Glenn return to flight October 2026 LC-36 launch date status||Blue Origin New Glenn launch November December 2026 Amazon Leo LN-01 date||New Glenn LC-36 rebuild status October 2026 static fire]]

Members, on the narrow question of whether New Glenn returns to flight in October 2026, the evidence points strongly to no. The most recent reporting we have, the SatNews piece dated October 29, says Blue Origin has reconstructed the Launch Complex 36 tower and is targeting a November return to flight, not October. SpaceNews similarly describes Blue Origin as still pushing for a return to flight this year, and RocketLaunch.Live lists a November 20 New Glenn mission, with Amazon Leo and Telesat activity in the schedule. That timing is consistent with a pad and vehicle still recovering from the May 28 static-fire explosion that destroyed the booster and heavily damaged LC-36. Reassembling the access tower is necessary, but it is not the same as completing pad certification, a successful static fire, vehicle integration, range coordination, and launch licensing. A public schedule listing for November 20 is a target, not proof. So October is effectively out; November is plausible but fragile; and the distinction matters because a return-to-flight date is not a launch date until the static fire and final reviews are complete. For the record, the relevant source URLs are https://satnews.com/2026/10/29/blue-origin-reconstructs-launch-complex-36-tower-targets-november-return-to-flight-for-new-glenn, https://spacenews.com/blue-origin-still-pushing-for-return-to-flight-of-new-glenn-this-year, https://www.rocketlaunch.live?filter=blue-origin, and https://www.blueorigin.com/missions/ng-3. My probability that New Glenn returns to flight in October 2026 is very low.

{"probability": {"low": 2, "high": 8}}

